{"issues":[{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"19756","self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/19756","key":"MC-272994","renderedFields":{"summary":null,"issuetype":null,"watches":null,"customfield_10070":null,"customfield_10061":"","created":"05/Jun/24 2:29 PM","customfield_10050":"","customfield_10051":null,"description":"<p>When attacking a mob with a fire aspect sword the sweeping affect can hit an assigned allay within range and light the allay on fire.</p>\n\n<p><b>What I expected to happen was...:</b><br>\nThe allay should be immune to damage from the player who owns it. This should prevent the allay from being affected by fire aspect.</p>\n\n<p><b>What actually happened was...:</b><br>\nWhen attacking a mob with the assigned allay nearby the allay does not appear to take damage from the sweeping affect but is still lit on fire.</p>\n\n<p><b>Steps to Reproduce:</b><br>\n1. Have an allay assigned to a player (give it an item).<br>\n2. Have a fire aspect sword.<br>\n3. Attack a mob with the fire aspect sword while the allay is in range of the sweeping effect.</p>","customfield_10054":null,"fixVersions":null,"customfield_10055":null,"resolution":null,"customfield_10047":"06/Jun/24 10:53 PM","customfield_10048":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10049":null,"attachment":[{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/35724","id":"35724","filename":"2024-06-06_13.48.10.png","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/62daf5e45eeecd39350a78a4/375b1309-50df-4bee-9c64-92412e684e27/48","24x24":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/62daf5e45eeecd39350a78a4/375b1309-50df-4bee-9c64-92412e684e27/24","16x16":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/62daf5e45eeecd39350a78a4/375b1309-50df-4bee-9c64-92412e684e27/16","32x32":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.